My transect lines are indeed bound by infrastructure causing a density gradient. This specific dataset was from the city centre. In this area the transect lines are flanked on both sides by tall buildings close to the road with no front gardens. Feral pigoens along the transects were either seen on the road and sidewalks or in the windowsills of the buildings along the transect. This resulted in more counts of pigeons along the 0-5 meter ranges due to the fact that the roads in my sampled city centre are very narrow.

