Hi Eric and thanks for your swift reply,

Having the protected area specific abundance estimate is
important to compare to prior surveys, that did not survey the three additional
strata in this most recent survey.

I ran detection function selection for the just the protect
area strata.  The best fitting model had
a different adjustment and produces an abundance estimate that was 23% higher
than the summed abundance for the protected area from the six strata model.  This estimate is also higher than the abundance
estimate across all six strata, which is not ideal for messaging.  Using the same detection function as for the
whole strata, which does not fit as well, produces an abundance estimate 11%
higher, which is still higher than the summed abundance for the protected area from
the six strata model.

When I try not using strata, this produces abundance estimates
40% higher for the best fitting model and 24% when using the same model that produced
the best fit for the full data set.

Thanks for your paper, I will try fitting the strata as a covariate shortly and feedback.

Cheers also for the pointer on finding the transect specific
estimates

Best,

Gwili

